+# Independent verification of CLAIM-delivery
+
+Revision checked: 187a0d76ab2bd14da51eea8c806d440011cf9914.
+Verifier: Codex, acting as the independent verifier of the supplied proof.
+Date: 2026-10-22.
+
+Inspected: [CLAIM-delivery](../CLAIM-delivery.md), its supplied
+[proof](proof.md), [deployment premises](../../verification/deployments.md),
+and the property statements, proofs, and current pass verdicts for
+[CLAIM-exclusive](../CLAIM-exclusive.md) and
+[CLAIM-failover](../CLAIM-failover.md).
+
+Attacks performed: preserved each imported claim's exact conditional
+conclusion; split the deployment into its two permitted modes; checked
+whether either case establishes the conjunction in CLAIM-delivery; checked
+whether the failed inference supplies an actual counterexample.
+
+The proof drops the imported mode conditions. CLAIM-exclusive supplies
+exclusivity only when mode is single-worker; CLAIM-failover supplies recovery
+only when mode is multi-worker. Their pass verdicts verify those conditional
+arguments, not unconditional properties. Mode is exactly one of these two
+values, so the premises needed to invoke both conclusions cannot hold in
+one deployment. In single-worker mode recovery is unsupported; in
+multi-worker mode exclusivity is unsupported.
+
+This is an incomplete composition argument, not an established delivery
+counterexample. A property outside an imported claim's scope may still hold.
+The deployment premises explicitly state that production implementation and
+an actual delivery counterexample are unavailable. Neither pass nor falsified
+is supported by the supplied evidence.
+
+A separate adversarial reviewer was requested but could not start because
+the agent tool failed to load its thread context. No separate-agent review
+was completed. No supplied property, proof, imported verdict, or executable
+verification was changed. No executable check establishes the missing
+cross-mode guarantees; the unrelated reservation SMT obligations were not run.
+
+To complete verification, supply evidence establishing both properties in
+the same deployment mode, retaining the exact claim and imported conditions.
